cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sylva: terrestrial and airborne laser scanning processing for forest ecology"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tim
    family-names: Devereux
    email: devereux.tj@gmail.com
    affiliation: The University of Queensland
repository-code: "https://github.com/UQ-EORC/Sylva"
url: "https://uq-eorc.github.io/Sylva/"
version: 0.3.0
abstract: >-
  Terrestrial and airborne laser scanning processing for forest ecology and
  remote sensing: ground classification, tree segmentation, quantitative
  structure models, ray-traced voxels, canopy metrics, coregistration,
  change detection and airborne lidar, with a Rust core, a Python API and a
  command-line tool.
keywords:
  - lidar
  - terrestrial laser scanning
  - airborne laser scanning
  - forest ecology
  - point cloud
  - quantitative structure model
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
year: 2026
